  "contentHtml": "\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <p><img src=\"https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/et-default-user.svg\" alt=\"Sudeep Lavania\">\n                                            \n                                        </p>\n                                                                        \n                                                                                    <ul>\n                                                                                                    <li>\n                                                                                                                                                                            <a>Sudeep Lavania</a>\n                                                            \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n                                                                                                            </li>\n                                                                                                                                                    <li><a href=\"/agency/87654367/TNN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TNN</a></li>\n                                                                                            </ul>\n                                                                                <ul>\n                                                                                            <li>Published On Sep 2, 2026 at 03:41 PM IST</li>\n                                                                                                                                </ul>\n                                    \n                                                                            \n                                                                        \n                                \n                                \n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p><a href=\"/tag/agra\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Agra</a>: Health department in Agra has issued a <a href=\"/tag/swine+flu+%28h1n1%29\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">swine flu (H1N1)</a> alert with screening of domestic and foreign tourists being stepped up at the city’s major tourism sites. It directed authorities to strictly implement the advisory issued by the UP govt.Officiating chief medical officer <a href=\"/tag/dr+amit+rawat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Dr Amit Rawat</a> on Tuesday said that vigilance has been increased in the city following swine flu cases in cities such as Delhi and Lucknow.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>“Given Agra’s status as a tourist destination, the health department has begun screening visitors at prominent sites, including <a href=\"/tag/taj+mahal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Taj Mahal</a> and <a href=\"/tag/fatehpur+sikri\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fatehpur Sikri</a>,” Rawat told TOI. Rawat added that an order for 5,000 <a href=\"/tag/tamiflu\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tamiflu</a> tablets had been placed to ensure that hospitals do not face a shortage of the antiviral medicine, if cases show up.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>Nodal officer Dr Surendra Mohan Prajapati said special wards and beds were kept reserved for swine flu patients at <a href=\"/tag/sn+medical+college\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SN Medical College</a> and the district hospital as a precautionary measure.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>Doctors at community health centres have also been given online training, while medical personnel at the district hospital and members of the <a href=\"/tag/rapid+response+team\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">rapid response team</a> have been administered the anti-swine flu vaccine.Health officials clarified that not every patient suffering from common cold, cough or fever would be tested for H1N1. Only patients showing severe symptoms would undergo swine flu testing.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>Health officials said children below 10 years, people above 70, pregnant women, and those suffering from conditions such as diabetes, cancer, tuberculosis, HIV/AIDS, blood disorders or diseases affecting the lungs, heart, kidneys or liver are considered more vulnerable to severe illness.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Sudeep Lavania</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Sudeep Lavania</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/87654367/TNN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TNN</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Sep 2, 2026 at 03:41 PM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Sep 2, 2026 at 03:41 PM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-subs__icon-nl\" role=\"presentation\" aria-label=\"Newsletter icon\">\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-newsletter.svg\" alt=\"Newsletter icon\" width=\"55\" height=\"55\">\n            </figure> -->\n        \n            \n                \n                    <h2>All about ETHealthworld industry right on your smartphone! </h2>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><a href=\"/app\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Download the ETHealthworld App</a> and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles.</li>\n                    </ul>\n                                            <!-- <div class=\"app-store-container desktop-view\">\n                            <a href=\"/app\" title=\"\" aria-label=\"Play Store\">\n                                <img loading=\"lazy\" width=\